Tests (required by acceptance + gate): apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/FSMHealthPanelTests.cs (27 tests)
  + FSMHealthPanel.Model.cs Compile-linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (headless net10.0 adapter/projection verification).

Web source parity (web/src/features/system/components/FSMHealthPanel.tsx):
  The web source is a PURE PRESENTATIONAL component: it derives health alerts from the resolved `transitions`
  prop in a useMemo and performs NO fetching, so there is no loading/error/stale/offline branch to reproduce
  (the parent StateMachineDebuggerPage owns the query) - mirrored exactly as the sibling presentational AuditPanel
  surface documents. Both web branches reproduced (every state renders - never a blank box):
    - all-clear (alerts.length === 0): TsGlassPanel -> green status dot + "All FSMs healthy ..." line.
    - alerts   (alerts.length  >  0): TsGlassPanel -> "FSM Health" title (Label typography) + responsive grid of cards.
  Detectors ported 1:1 in the web's order (flap -> stuck -> recovery):
    - flap: >5 same-fsm transitions within a 60s window; the alert COUNT is captured at the first flapping FSM
      (the web pushes the alert inside the per-FSM loop), while ComputeFlapIds returns the UNION across all FSMs
      (the web's exported computeFlapIds helper) - both behaviours covered by tests.
    - stuck: latest transition per `fsm_name:vehicle_id` for drive_session/charge_session in pending/active > 4h
      (reference instant injected for deterministic tests).
    - recovery: count of transitions whose to_state === "recovered".
  Shared components mapped: @/components/ui GlassPanel -> TsGlassPanel, the web <h2> title -> Label typography
    (uppercase/tracking-wider/secondary role); @/components/layout Grid -> responsive WinUI Grid reflow
    (1 column < md / one column per alert >= md, mirroring web cols={{ default: 1, md: alerts.length }}).
  Charts / maps: none (the web source uses none).
  Severity tints from the W1 status tokens (NOT ported Tailwind): warning -> TsColorWarning*, info -> TsColorInfo*,
    all-clear -> TsColorSuccess*; border/fill at the web's /20 and /5 opacities. Glyphs -> Segoe Fluent
    (AlertTriangle -> Warning E7BA, Timer E916, RotateCw -> Refresh E72C). Count rendered via NumberFormatting
    (the web fmtInt); the message {0} token (the catalog's port of the web {{count}}) interpolated with the same formatter.
  i18n: all 8 labels resolve through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade - translation.fsm.health.{title, allClear,
    flapTitle, stuckTitle, recoveryTitle, flapping, stuck, recoveries}. The keys ALREADY EXIST in the
    auto-generated Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw catalog (verified present); not hand-edited (the generator
    stores the web {{count}} as the .NET {0} token). Catalog-key flow asserted via a PrefixLocalizer test.
  Accessibility: Narrator name on the panel and on every alert card; decorative glyphs marked AccessibilityView.Raw;
    TextBlock honours the system font-scale factor (default); no motion (reduce-motion trivially honoured).
  Telemetry: FsmHealthPanelDiagnostics emits "view.opened slug=FSMHealthPanel" (PII-safe) on first load (P1/S11).

